{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Subword Tokenization \u2014 BPE, WordPiece, Unigram, SentencePiece Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: BPE from scratch"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "See `code/main.py`. The loop:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def train_bpe(corpus, num_merges):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    vocab = {tuple(word) + (\"</w>\",): count for word, count in corpus.items()}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    merges = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for _ in range(num_merges):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        pairs = Counter()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for symbols, freq in vocab.items():"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for a, b in zip(symbols, symbols[1:]):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                pairs[(a, b)] += freq"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if not pairs:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            break"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        best = pairs.most_common(1)[0][0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        merges.append(best)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        vocab = apply_merge(vocab, best)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return merges"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Three facts the algorithm encodes. `</w>` marks word end so \"low\" (suffix) and \"lower\" (prefix) stay distinct. Frequency weighting makes high-frequency pairs win early. The merge list is ordered \u2014 inference applies merges in training order."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: encode with the learned merges"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def encode_bpe(word, merges):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    symbols = list(word) + [\"</w>\"]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for a, b in merges:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        i = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        while i < len(symbols) - 1:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if symbols[i] == a and symbols[i + 1] == b:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                symbols = symbols[:i] + [a + b] + symbols[i + 2:]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                i += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return symbols"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Naive O(n\u00b7|merges|). Production implementations (tiktoken, HF Tokenizers) use merge-rank lookup with priority queues and run in near-linear time."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: SentencePiece in practice"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import sentencepiece as spm"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "spm.SentencePieceTrainer.train("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    input=\"corpus.txt\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    model_prefix=\"my_tokenizer\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    vocab_size=8000,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    model_type=\"bpe\",          # or \"unigram\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    character_coverage=0.9995, # lower for CJK (e.g. 0.9995 for English, 0.995 for Japanese)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    normalization_rule_name=\"nmt_nfkc\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "sp = spm.SentencePieceProcessor(model_file=\"my_tokenizer.model\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(sp.encode(\"untokenizable\", out_type=str))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# ['\u2581un', 'token', 'izable']"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Notice: no pre-tokenization required, space encoded as `\u2581`, `character_coverage` controls how aggressively rare characters are preserved vs mapped to `<unk>`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: tiktoken for OpenAI-compatible vocabs"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import tiktoken"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "enc = tiktoken.get_encoding(\"o200k_base\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(enc.encode(\"untokenizable\"))        # [127340, 101028]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(len(enc.encode(\"Hello, world!\")))   # 4"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Encoding-only. Fast (Rust backend). Exact match with GPT-4/5 tokenization for byte-counting, cost estimation, context-window budgeting."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Train a 500-merge BPE on `code/main.py`'s tiny corpus. Encode three held-out words. How many produced exactly 1 token vs >1 token?\n2. **Medium.** Compare token counts on 100 English Wikipedia sentences between `cl100k_base`, `o200k_base`, and a SentencePiece BPE you train with vocab=32k. Report the compression ratio of each.\n3. **Hard.** Train the same corpus with BPE, Unigram, and WordPiece. Measure downstream accuracy when using each on a small sentiment classifier. Does the choice move the needle by more than 1 point F1?"
      ]
    }
